  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In October 2025 remarks, Christopher J. Waller framed AI’s labor effects as a question of whether it replaces people or makes them more productive, and said policymakers must separate hype from data to understand AI’s implications for growth, productivity, and the economy. He also stated that if AI constitutes a structural shift in labor demand, monetary policy will not be an effective tool. In September 2026, he discussed whether agentic commerce will use platform-specific or interoperable standards, saying interoperable standards could help level the playing field for smaller merchants and payment providers. He called for a proactive approach that balances innovation with safety, integrity, and stability in payments.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5"
   ],
